INTERPRETATION
At K=2Q+1 the reflection-odd quotient is the simple-current
permutation V -> Q-V.  A single crossing column therefore has only a
same and a reflected terminal endpoint.  With x=V-1 and y=Q-V, the
program reconstructs both endpoint margins as the displayed
nonnegative slack polynomials.  It independently checks the
Kac--Walton formula against the quotient recurrence through Q=100.

